The compensation awarded by the Tribunal towards attendant,
conveyance, food and nourishment charges in a sum of Rs.20,000/- is just and proper;
9.6.

In all other respects, the judgment and award of the Tribunal remains unaltered;
iii) The appellant/claimant is entitled to an enhanced compensation of Rs.8,55,000/-
together with interest at 7% per annum from the date of the petition till its realization, except for a period of 189 days, in addition to the compensation awarded by the Tribunal;
iv) Out of the enhanced compensation together with accrued interest, 50% shall be kept in a fixed deposit in a Nationalized Bank of the choice of the claimant for the period of three years, upon the expiry of which period the said fixed deposit amount together with the accrued interest shall be directly released to the claimant without any further orders from the Tribunal or from this Court in this regard.

